    I stopped here to mention this because:
    Joseph Fourier derived this system of equations
    while studying the propagation of heat in a metal rod.
    So everywhere we use time as a variable,
    Joseph had a one-dimensional space.
    Since his experiment consisted in applying heat in the middle of the rod
    and studying the dissipation in both directions,
    splitting T₀ in half was actually the straightforward move from his perspective.
